Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|custom.properties|default.layout.template.id=1_column${line.separator}company.default.time.zone=America/Los_Angeles|
		|testray.main.component.name|Calendar|
	And these variables
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|custom.properties|default.layout.template.id=1_column${line.separator}company.default.time.zone=America/Los_Angeles|
		|testray.main.component.name|Calendar|
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
		|portletName|Calendar|
Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG
	And Page add
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	Then Portlet add PG
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
		|portletName|Calendar|
Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: View Correct Number Of Weeks Month View
Priority: 3
##########################################################
The Poshi description element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
	When Calendar view Month
		|dateMonth|April 2016|
	And Calendar view Week Count Via Month View
		|weekNumber|5|
	And Calendar view Month
		|dateMonth|July 2016|
	Then Calendar view Week Count Via Month View
		|weekNumber|6|
Scenario: View Created Event Visible On Scheduler
Priority: 2
##########################################################
The Poshi description element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
	When CalendarNavigator goto Add Event
	And these variables
		|endDateTime||
	And these variables
		|startDateTime||
	And CalendarEvent view Times
		|endDateTime|${endDateTime}|
		|startDateTime|${startDateTime}|
	And CalendarEvent edit Title
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event|
	And CalendarEvent publish
	And IFrame close Frame
	Then CalendarScheduler select Specific Event
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event|
Scenario: View Default Durations Via Scheduler
Priority: 3
	Given Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	When CalendarNavigator goto Configuration
	And CalendarConfiguration select Default Duration
		|defaultDuration|15 Minutes|
	And CalendarConfiguration save
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto View
		|viewType|Day|
	And CalendarEvent add Via Day View
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 15 Minutes Title|
	And CalendarScheduler view Event Duration
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 15 Minutes Title|
		|minutes|15|
	And CalendarEvent tear Down
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto Configuration
	And CalendarConfiguration select Default Duration
		|defaultDuration|30 Minutes|
	And CalendarConfiguration save
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto View
		|viewType|Day|
	And CalendarEvent add Via Day View
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 30 Minutes Title|
	And CalendarScheduler view Event Duration
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 30 Minutes Title|
		|minutes|30|
	And CalendarEvent tear Down
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto Configuration
	And CalendarConfiguration select Default Duration
		|defaultDuration|60 Minutes|
	And CalendarConfiguration save
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto View
		|viewType|Day|
	And CalendarEvent add Via Day View
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 60 Minutes Title|
	And CalendarScheduler view Event Duration
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 60 Minutes Title|
		|minutes|60|
	And CalendarEvent tear Down
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto Configuration
	And CalendarConfiguration select Default Duration
		|defaultDuration|120 Minutes|
	And CalendarConfiguration save
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto View
		|viewType|Day|
	And CalendarEvent add Via Day View
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 120 Minutes Title|
	And CalendarScheduler view Event Duration
		|eventTitle|Calendar Event 120 Minutes Title|
		|minutes|120|
	Then CalendarEvent tear Down
Scenario: View Displayed Site Calendar Events As Guest
Priority: 3
##########################################################
The Poshi description element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
	When these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|CalendarScheduler#ViewDisplayedSiteCalendarEventsAsGuest|
	And TestCase get Site Name
##########################################################
The Poshi return element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	And CalendarNavigator goto Add Event
	And CalendarEvent edit Title
		|eventTitle|Liferay Calendar Event Title|
	And CalendarEvent set Times
		|endDateTime|04:00 AM|
		|startDateTime|03:00 AM|
	And CalendarEvent select Calendar
		|calendarName|${siteName}|
	And CalendarEvent publish
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarNavigator goto Add Event
	And CalendarEvent edit Title
		|eventTitle|Test Test Calendar Event Title|
	And CalendarEvent set Times
		|endDateTime|09:00 PM|
		|startDateTime|08:00 PM|
	And CalendarEvent select Calendar
		|calendarName|Test Test|
	And CalendarEvent publish
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarScheduler view Week
		|eventTitle|Liferay Calendar Event Title|
	And CalendarScheduler view Week
		|eventTitle|Test Test Calendar Event Title|
	And ProductMenu goto Personal Site
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Calendar|
	And User logout PG
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And CalendarEvent view Site Calendar Event With Default Permissions
		|calendarName|${siteName}|
		|endDateTime|04:00 AM|
		|eventTitle|Liferay Calendar Event Title|
		|siteName|${siteName}|
		|startDateTime|03:00 AM|
	And CalendarEvent view Site Calendar Event Not Present
		|endDateTime|09:00 PM|
		|siteName|Test Test|
		|startDateTime|08:00 PM|
	And Navigator goto Specific URL Page
		|pageName|Welcome|
		|url|localhost:8080/web/test|
	And CalendarEvent view Site Calendar Event With Default Permissions
		|calendarName|Test Test|
		|endDateTime|09:00 PM|
		|eventTitle|Test Test Calendar Event Title|
		|siteName|Test Test|
		|startDateTime|08:00 PM|
	Then CalendarEvent view Site Calendar Event Not Present
		|endDateTime|04:00 AM|
		|siteName|${siteName}|
		|startDateTime|03:00 AM|

